      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To truly convey that hopelessness, have Elias observe the performance from a cold, detached distance, as if watching a poorly acted play starring himself. Let his internal monologue acknowledge the *logic* of giving up, not just the emotion. He shouldn't just feel hopeless; he should feel logically correct in concluding that the effort required outweighs any possible return. This intellectual surrender is often scarier than simple sadness.",
      "source": "target",
